<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" ?>

<!--
	Pictures in a view: where a picture comes from, how it is fitted into a box, and how content is
	stacked over it.
	
	The first section takes the picture from a channel: the table selects a flow node, the "photo"
	channel maps it onto the binary attribute holding its PNG, and the <image> beside the table
	shows it. Its resource is the placeholder that fills the box while nothing is selected. The
	overlay around it stacks a badge in the upper corner and a caption along the lower edge over the
	same picture; both layers take their position from the <layer>, and their look from the
	application stylesheet (style/tl-demo-react.css). The avatar reads the same photo channel and
	crops it into a circle; the avatar beside it reads no picture channel and therefore stays at the
	initials of the selected node. The second picture shows the same data fitted into the box
	instead of cropped to fill it.
	
	The second section shows a resource of the web application alone - the file under /images, with
	no channel behind it.
	
	The third section loads the address that is typed into the field. The channel starts out at this
	application's own landscape, so the section shows a picture at once; the field writes through to
	it, and an empty field answers that address again.
-->
<view>
	<channels>
		<channel name="node"/>
		<derived-channel name="photo"
			expr="n -> $n.get(`test.flowchart:FlowNode#image`)"
			inputs="node"
		/>
		<!--
			What the user typed, and the address shown for it: the derived channel answers the
			application's own picture while nothing is typed and writes what is typed back, so the
			input field and the picture share one value.
		-->
		<channel name="urlInput"/>
		<derived-channel name="url"
			expr="u -> if($u == null || $u.isEmpty(), contextPath() + '/images/demo-landscape.svg', $u)"
			inputs="urlInput"
			reverse="u -> $u"
		/>
	</channels>

	<panel>
		<title>
			<en>Images</en>
			<de>Bilder</de>
		</title>

		<text>
			<label>
				<en>A picture from a channel</en>
				<de>Ein Bild aus einem Kanal</de>
			</label>
		</text>
		<text>
			<label>
				<en>Select a flow node: its picture appears in the box beside the table, with a badge in the corner and a caption along the lower edge stacked over it. Without a selection the box shows the placeholder resource. The two boxes have the same proportions; the upper one crops the picture to fill them, the lower one fits the whole picture into them. The left avatar shows the same picture in a circle, the right one the initials it falls back to without a picture.</en>
				<de>Wählen Sie einen Flow-Knoten: Sein Bild erscheint im Rahmen neben der Tabelle, darüber ein Abzeichen in der Ecke und eine Bildunterschrift an der Unterkante. Ohne Auswahl zeigt der Rahmen die Platzhalter-Ressource. Beide Rahmen haben dieselben Proportionen; der obere beschneidet das Bild, der untere zeigt es vollständig. Der linke Avatar zeigt dasselbe Bild im Kreis, der rechte die Initialen, auf die er ohne Bild zurückfällt.</de>
			</label>
		</text>

		<grid
			gap="default"
			max-columns="2"
			min-column-width="20rem"
		>
			<table
				observed-types="test.flowchart:FlowNode"
				selection="node"
				types="test.flowchart:FlowNode"
			>
				<columns>
					<column attribute="name"/>
				</columns>
				<rows>all(`test.flowchart:FlowNode`)</rows>
			</table>
			<!--
				The column does not stretch its children: an overlay stretched past its base would
				anchor its layers to the free space beside the picture rather than to the picture.
			-->
			<stack
				align="start"
				direction="column"
				gap="default"
			>
				<overlay>
					<image
						aspect-ratio="4/3"
						fit="cover"
						input="photo"
						resource="/images/no-picture.svg"
						width="20rem"
					>
						<alt>
							<en>The picture of the selected flow node.</en>
							<de>Das Bild des gewählten Flow-Knotens.</de>
						</alt>
					</image>
					<layer
						css-class="tlDemoBadge"
						position="top-left"
					>
						<text>
							<label>
								<en>Preview</en>
								<de>Vorschau</de>
							</label>
						</text>
					</layer>
					<layer
						css-class="tlDemoCaption"
						position="bottom"
					>
						<text input="node"/>
					</layer>
				</overlay>
				<stack
					align="center"
					direction="row"
					gap="default"
				>
					<avatar
						image="photo"
						input="node"
						size="xl"
					/>
					<avatar
						input="node"
						size="xl"
					/>
					<image
						aspect-ratio="4/3"
						fit="contain"
						input="photo"
						width="20rem"
					/>
				</stack>
			</stack>
		</grid>

		<text>
			<label>
				<en>A resource of the web application</en>
				<de>Eine Ressource der Web-Anwendung</de>
			</label>
		</text>
		<text>
			<label>
				<en>The file /images/demo-landscape.svg, shown without any channel behind it. The path is resolved against the context path of the application.</en>
				<de>Die Datei /images/demo-landscape.svg, ohne Kanal dahinter. Der Pfad wird gegen den Kontextpfad der Anwendung aufgelöst.</de>
			</label>
		</text>
		<image
			resource="/images/demo-landscape.svg"
			width="16rem"
		>
			<alt>
				<en>A landscape of a few shapes.</en>
				<de>Eine Landschaft aus wenigen Formen.</de>
			</alt>
		</image>

		<text>
			<label>
				<en>An address the user enters</en>
				<de>Eine eingegebene Adresse</de>
			</label>
		</text>
		<text>
			<label>
				<en>The picture is loaded by the browser from the address on the channel; the box keeps its proportions whatever the picture measures, and the browser postpones the loading until the box comes into view.</en>
				<de>Das Bild wird vom Browser von der Adresse aus dem Kanal geladen; der Rahmen behält seine Proportionen, gleich welche Maße das Bild hat, und der Browser lädt es erst, wenn der Rahmen in Sichtweite kommt.</de>
			</label>
		</text>
		<fields>
			<value-input
				type="tl.core:String"
				value="url"
			>
				<label>
					<en>Image URL</en>
					<de>Bildadresse</de>
				</label>
			</value-input>
		</fields>
		<image
			aspect-ratio="16/9"
			fit="contain"
			input="url"
			lazy="true"
			width="24rem"
		/>
	</panel>
</view>